==English==
{{was wotd|2024|November|3}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/səˈtɔːɹi/|/sæ-/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-satori.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/səˈtɔɹi/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːɹi|s=3}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sa|to|ri}}

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ja|悟り|tr=satori|t=understanding; (''Buddhism'') enlightenment, satori}}, from {{m|ja|悟る|tr=satoru|t=to perceive; to comprehend, understand; to come to enlightenment}}, from {{der|en|ltc|悟|tr=nguH|t=to become aware, apprehend, realize; to awaken}} (modern {{cog|cmn|悟}}), used to translate {{noncog|pi|bodhi|t=supreme knowledge}} or its {{glossary|etymon}} {{noncog|sa|बोधि|t=perfect knowledge or wisdom by which a person becomes a buddha or jina; enlightened or illuminated intellect of a Buddha or jina}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=5684330061|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

{{senseno|en|gene|uc=1}} (“mutant gene of ''Drosophila'' that causes homosexual behaviour in males”) was {{coinage|en|Daisuke Yamamoto|w=-|nat=the Japanese|occ=scientist|nobycat=1|nocap=1}} in a 1991 paper,<ref>{{cite-web|author=Daisuke Yamamoto|title=Nature vs. Nurture in Drosophila Courtship [abstract of a lecture]|work=w:Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology|url=https://groups.oist.jp/ja/fao/event/nature-vs-nurture-drosophila-courtship-prof-daisuke-yamamoto<!--Currently unable to archive this at the Internet Archive-->|date=30 March 2016|passage=Approximately 25 years ago, I discovered a clue to tackling this problem by isolating a ''Drosophila'' mutant that I named ''satori'', males of which preferentially courted males rather than females without copulating (Yamamoto et al., 1991)<!--Article not fully identified in abstract-->.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241201024500/https://groups.oist.jp/ja/fao/event/nature-vs-nurture-drosophila-courtship-prof-daisuke-yamamoto|archivedate=1 December 2024}}</ref> based on the Japanese term.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|[[Zen]]|_|Buddhism}} A [[sudden]] [[inexpressible]] [[feeling#Noun|feeling]] of [[spiritual awakening]] or [[enlightenment]], the [[result#Noun|result]] of [[meditation]] and [[study#Noun|study]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1727|author=Engelbertus Kæmpfer [''i.e.'', {{w|Engelbert Kaempfer}}]|chapter=Of the Temples and Clergy of this City|translator=J. G. Scheuchzer [''i.e.'', {{w|Johann Caspar Scheuchzer}}]|title=The History of Japan,{{nb...|Giving an Account of the Ancient and Present State and Government of that Empire; of Its Temples, Palaces, Castles and Other Buildings; of Its Metals, Minerals, Trees, Plants, Animals, Birds and Fishes; of the Chronology and Succession of the Emperors, Ecclesiastical and Secular; of the Original Descent, Religions, Customs, and Manufactures of the Natives, and of Their Trade and Commerce with the Dutch and Chinese. Together with a Description of the Kingdom of Siam. Written in High-Dutch by Engelbertus Kæmpfer, M.D. Physician to the Dutch Embassy to the Emperor’s Court; and Translated from His Original Manuscript, Never before Printed, by J. G. Scheuchzer, F.R.S. and a Member of the College of Physicians, London. With the Life of the Author, and an Introduction. Illustrated with Many Copper Plates}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed}} [F]or the translator|volume=I|section=book IV (Of Nagasacki,{{nb...|the Place of Residence for Foreigners: Of Their Trade, Accommodation, &c.}})|page=308|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/historyofjapangi01kaem/page/308/mode/1up|oclc=1077878153|passage=[B]y his ſublime underſtanding and reputed great knovvledge in divine myſteries he obtain'd, and ſtill keeps, the name and repute of a ''Godo'', that is, a perſon bleſs'd vvith a divine and moſt accute underſtanding, vvhom they ſuppoſe to be able to find out by his '''''Satori''''', or Enthuſiaſtic Speculations, ſuch miſterious truths, as are far beyond the reach of common knovvledge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1727|author=Engelbertus Kæmpfer [''i.e.'', {{w|Engelbert Kaempfer}}]|chapter=[The Appendix{{nb...|to the History of Japan}}.] I. The Natural History of the Japanese Tea; with an Accurate Description of that Plant, Its Culture, Growth, Preparation, and Uses.|translator=J. G. Scheuchzer [''i.e.'', {{w|Johann Caspar Scheuchzer}}]|title=The History of Japan,{{nb...|Giving an Account of the Ancient and Present State and Government of that Empire; of Its Temples, Palaces, Castles and Other Buildings; of Its Metals, Minerals, Trees, Plants, Animals, Birds and Fishes; of the Chronology and Succession of the Emperors, Ecclesiastical and Secular; of the Original Descent, Religions, Customs, and Manufactures of the Natives, and of Their Trade and Commerce with the Dutch and Chinese. Together with a Description of the Kingdom of Siam. Written in High-Dutch by Engelbertus Kæmpfer, M.D. Physician to the Dutch Embassy to the Emperor’s Court; and Translated from His Original Manuscript, Never before Printed, by J. G. Scheuchzer, F.R.S. and a Member of the College of Physicians, London. With the Life of the Author, and an Introduction. Illustrated with Many Copper Plates}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed}} [F]or the translator|volume=II|section=§&nbsp;2|page=3|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/historyofjapangi02kaem/page/3/mode/1up|oclc=1077878153|passage=He {{quote-gloss|Darma or {{w|Bodhidharma}}}} lived only upon vegetables, and thought this to be the higheſt degree of Holineſs, to paſs days and nights in an uninterrupted '''''Satori''''', that is, a contemplation of the Divine Being.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1962|author=[[w:Philip K. Dick|Philip K[indred] Dick]]|chapter=3|title=w:The Man in the High Castle|edition=1st {{w|Mariner Books}}|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Houghton Mifflin Harcourt|Houghton Mifflin Harcourt Publishing Company]]|year_published=2011|page=31|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=NtukmPtq2l8C&pg=PA31|isbn=978-0-547-57248-2|passage="Slim your hips the Zen way," Juliana said. "Lose pounds through painless '''satori'''. I'm sorry, Miss Davis. I'm woolgathering."}}
#* {{RQ:T. Wolfe Acid Test|chapter=VIII|page=102|passage=It was as if [[w:Neal Cassady|{{quote-gloss|Neal}} Cassady]] {{...}} was in a state of '''satori''', as totally into this very moment, Now, as a being can get.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=w:Kōshō Uchiyama|chapter=The World of Intensive Practice|translators=Daitsu Tom [Thomas] Wright; w:Jisho Warner; [[w:Shōhaku Okumura|Shohaku Okumura]]|title=Opening the Hand of Thought: Foundations of Zen Buddhist Practice|location=Somerville, Mass.|publisher=[[w:Foundation for the Preservation of the Mahayana Tradition|Wisdom Publications]]|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=okE6AwAAQBAJ&pg=PA68|page=68|isbn=978-0-86171-357-8|passage='''Satori''' and Zen seem to have such an intimate relationship in Japan that when somebody says "'''satori'''," everybody immediately associates it with Zen, and vice versa. {{...}} For [[w:The Buddha|Shakyamuni]], '''satori''' wasn't something peculiar only to himself. His was the '''satori''' of life inclusive of himself and all things. That is something that truly goes beyond the discrimination of our minds.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|figurative}} Enlightenment, [[epiphany]].
#* {{RQ:Torgoff Can't Find My Way Home|page=115|passage=What happened to the Merry Band on its trip during the summer of 1964 ranged from the cosmically sublime to the ridiculous, from peak ecstasy to full-tilt '''satori'''. To say that they were merely high would do a disservice to how stoned they really were, {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|gene}}{{lb|en|countable|biochemistry}} A [[mutant#Adjective|mutant]] [[gene]] of {{taxfmt|Drosophila|genus}}, a [[genus]] of [[fruit fly|fruit flies]], that [[cause#Verb|causes]] [[homosexual#Adjective|homosexual]] [[behavior|behaviour]] in [[male#Noun|males]] (specifically, [[courtship]] [[direct#Verb|directed]] to other males).
#: {{synonyms|en|sat<q:abbreviation>}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1996|month=September|author=Hiroki Ito; Daisuke Yamamoto [''et al.'']|title=Sexual Orientation in ''Drosophila'' is Altered by the Satori Mutation in the Sex-determination Gene Fruitless that Encodes a Zinc Finger Protein with a BTB Domain|journal=w:Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240930050011/https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC38490/|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=w:National Academy of Sciences|volume=93|issue=18|page=9687|column=1|doi=10.1073/pnas.93.18.9687|issn=0027-8424|jstor=00278424|oclc=35912523|pmid=8790392|passage=We have isolated a new ''Drosophila'' mutant, '''satori''' (''sat''), the males of which do not court or copulate with female flies. {{...}} We have screened about 2000 fly lines with single P-element insertions for altered sexual behavior, yielding a mutant named '''satori''' (''sat''; nirvana in Japanese), the males of which do not court or copulate with females. Instead, ''sat'' males exhibit homosexual courtship.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1996|month=October|author=Daisuke Yamamoto; Hiroki Ito; Kazuko Fujitani|title=Genetic Dissection of Sexual Orientation: Behavioral, Cellular, and Molecular Approaches in ''Drosophila melanogaster''|journal=Neuroscience Research: The Official Journal of the Japan Neuroscience Society|location=Amsterdam|publisher=[[w:Elsevier|Elsevier Science]]|volume=26|issue=2|section=abstract|page=95|doi=10.1016/S0168-0102(96)01087-5|issn=0168-0102|oclc=644550050|passage=[T]he primary site of action of the ''fru'' gene should be in the neural cells. '''''satori''''',{{sic}} one of the P-insertion alleles of ''fru'' which we isolated, carried the ''lacZ'' gene of ''E. coli'' as a reporter, and β-galactosidase expression was found in a subset of brain cells including those in the antennal lobe in the '''''satori''''' mutant.}}

